# Warning: Open `app/backend` for variables to work. Or save variables (see
# below) in a settings.json file in your workspace's .vscode folder.
# 
# Setup:
# 1. Install REST Client extension for VS Code.
# 2. Duplicate .vscode/settings.json.template to .vscode/settings.json
# 3. Add environment variable values.
#    - For Notion variables, follow 'Notion setup' steps below.
#
# Usage:
# 1. Set environment:
#      * Cmd (⇧⌘P) > Rest Client: Switch Environment
#      * This will fix red lines.
# 2. Quick navigation
#      * Search (⌘P) > '@'

### ----------------------------------------------------
### Pocketbase API
### ----------------------------------------------------
### List all blocks
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/{{block_collection_id}}/records HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: {{auth_token}}

### Create waiting Block Job
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/{{block_job_collection_id}}/records HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: {{auth_token}}

{
    "status": "waiting",
    "type": "transcription",
    "block": "hyi1k9zhajjxxx8",
    "user": "{{user_id}}",
    "summary": ["initial value"]
}

### Create audio block
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/{{block_collection_id}}/records HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"
Content-Type: application/json

audio
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"
Content-Type: application/json

block title
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="user"
Content-Type: application/json

{{user_id}}
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="jfk.wav"
Content-Type: audio/wav

< jfk.wav
--boundary--

### ----------------------------------------------------
### Notion API
### ----------------------------------------------------
### Notion setup 1/2: Get code
# 1. Get client ID for the Exnota Notion Integration (see relevant vault)
# 2. Add it to this URL: https://api.notion.com/v1/oauth/authorize?client_id={{notionOauthClientId}}&response_type=code&owner=user&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fexnota.com%2Fapi%2Fintegration%2Fnotion%2Fmobile-code-redirect
# 3. Open in browser AND START CAPTURING NETWORK REQUESTS
# 4. Go through flow, and get code from attempted redirect
#    (won't actually redirect due to exnota:// scheme).

### Notion setup 2/2: Get access token, workspace_id, bot_id, owner user id.
# 1. Get code from previous step.
# 2. Replace "a code" below with this code.
POST {{baseUrl}}/notion-token HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json

{
    "code": "a code"
}

### blocks - append file block
curl -X PATCH 'https://api.notion.com/v1/blocks/2daf121ec2e742299da72e1df4eb67b9/children' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer '"{{notionAccessToken}}"'' \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Notion-Version: 2022-06-28" \
  --data '{
	"children": [
		{
			"object": "block",
			"type": "file",
			"file": {
				"caption": [],
				"type": "external",
				"external": {
					"url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/JFK_inaugural_address.ogg"
				}
			}
		}
	]
}'

### ----------------------------------------------------
### OpenAI Whisper
### ----------------------------------------------------

### Transcribe
POST https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/transcriptions
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary
Authorization: Bearer {{openAiKey}}

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="model"
Content-Type: application/json

whisper-1
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="short-test.m4a"
Content-Type: audio/x-m4a

< short-test.m4a
--boundary--
